  <!-- ⚠️ STUB — PREMISES NOT YET VERIFIED. Author with /task-create. Note task 106 moved these lines,
       so any line number quoted below is already suspect. See notes/task-accuracy-audit-2026-09-18.md. -->

  <prompt>`GrantExternalAccessEndpoint.CreateGrantAsync` reads the key's active rows, elects a survivor, then deactivates the rest — with NO ETag or conditional update between the read and the write. Task 106 changed the election key from an IMMUTABLE row id to a MUTABLE `sprk_expiresdate` read at T₀, which makes one new outcome reachable: rows r₁ (expires today+10, lower id) and r₂ (today+200); a date-less grant elects r₂; concurrently `/set-record-share-expiry` moves r₂ to today+1; the grant then collapses onto r₂ — now the shorter row — and deactivates r₁. Access was conferred until +10 before the call and until +1 after.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer, C#/.NET, the external grant lifecycle.</role>
  <goal>A duplicate collapse cannot apply to a row whose state changed since the read, so a concurrent expiry change cannot shorten conferred access and a concurrent revoke cannot leave the key with zero active rows.</goal>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="register ISS-022">Task 106's V1 fix does NOT address this. V1 removed request-DEPENDENCE from the ranking; this is about the ranked column being MUTABLE. Do not assume the election is the problem.</constraint>
    <constraint source="register ISS-022">Honest scope: only the SHORTENING shape is new. The revoke-race variant (a racer deactivates the elected row, then the collapse removes the others, leaving zero rows) is PRE-EXISTING and symmetric — pre-106 it fired whenever the revoked row was the lowest id. Fix both or state which is out of scope.</constraint>
    <constraint source="task 106">Do NOT reintroduce request-dependence into the election. `ElectSurvivor` deliberately takes no request value so request-independence is structural; a concurrency fix must not undo that (perturbation P5 pins it).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-003">Fail closed: an outcome the endpoint cannot verify is never reported as success.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <notes>Suggested fix on file: `If-Match` on the row's ETag for the deactivation — the read-then-write pair has no optimistic concurrency at all. A re-read immediately before the collapse narrows but does not close the window. Register: `notes/defer-issues.md` § ISS-022. Related: tasks 010, 023, 098, 106.</notes>
</task>
